@startuml UC39_43_Fulfillment_Sequence
title UC-39–43 — User to database flows in the current backend
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam ParticipantPadding 18
skinparam BoxPadding 8

actor "Accountant / Shop Owner / Shipper" as User
participant "Frontend\nBrowser / Mobile UI" as UI
participant "Spring Security\nJWT resource-server filters" as Sec
participant "Fulfillment Controller\n(UC-specific REST endpoint)" as Ctrl
participant "DeliveryIssueService" as Issue
participant "DeliveryService" as DeliverySvc
participant "IAM API\ncurrent user / shipper lookup" as IAM
participant "Sales OrderDispatchApi" as Sales
participant "CatalogApi" as Catalog
participant "Stock APIs\nInventoryApi + Reservation API" as Stock
participant "Finance API\nDeliveryCodCapacityApi" as Finance
participant "Repositories / stores\nJPA + JdbcTemplate" as Repo
database "PostgreSQL\ndeliveries, delivery_items,\nstock/reservation/payment tables" as DB
participant "DeliveryPhotoStorage\nlocal filesystem adapter" as Photos

== UC-39: choose an issued invoice, inspect candidates, create draft ==
User -> UI: Select order and delivery action
UI -> Sec: GET /api/v1/fulfillment/orders/{orderId}/delivery-invoices\nAuthorization: Bearer JWT
Sec -> Sec: Validate JWT, role ACCOUNTANT or SHOP_OWNER
Sec -> Ctrl: Authorized request
Ctrl -> Issue: issuedInvoices(orderId)
Issue -> IAM: getCurrentUser()
IAM --> Issue: authenticated actor ID / roles
Issue -> Sales: read(orderId); issuedInvoices(orderId)
Sales -> DB: Read order and ISSUED invoice summaries
DB --> Sales: order + invoice rows
Sales --> Issue: invoice summaries
Issue --> Ctrl: summaries
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<List<InvoiceSummary>>
UI --> User: Show issued invoices

User -> UI: Select invoice; open delivery candidates
UI -> Sec: GET /sales-invoices/{invoiceId}/delivery-candidates
Sec -> Ctrl: Authorized request
Ctrl -> Issue: invoiceCandidates(invoiceId)
Issue -> IAM: getCurrentUser()
Issue -> Sales: invoice(invoiceId); read(orderId)
Issue -> Repo: issuedForInvoice(invoiceId); issued(orderId)
Repo -> DB: SELECT delivery_items JOIN deliveries\nconfirmed_at IS NOT NULL
DB --> Repo: already issued quantities
Issue -> Stock: findByOrder(orderId); getStockSummary(variantId)
Stock -> DB: Read reservation and stock snapshots
DB --> Stock: held / available quantity
Issue -> Catalog: getSkuSummary(variantId)
Catalog -> DB: Read SKU serial-tracking metadata
DB --> Catalog: SKU summary
Issue --> Ctrl: Candidate quantities, stock, serial flag, eligibility
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<Candidates>
UI --> User: Show invoice-bound candidate lines

User -> UI: Submit draft (client-generated deliveryId)
UI -> Sec: POST /sales-invoices/{invoiceId}/deliveries
Sec -> Ctrl: Authorized request
Ctrl -> Issue: createFromInvoice(invoiceId, request)
Issue -> IAM: getCurrentUser()
Issue -> Repo: lockRequest(deliveryId)
Repo -> DB: pg_advisory_xact_lock(...)
Issue -> Sales: lock(orderId); lockInvoice(invoiceId)
Sales -> DB: Lock/read order and invoice rows
DB --> Sales: PROCESSING order + ISSUED invoice
Issue -> Repo: Check replay, issued totals, next batch number
Repo -> DB: SELECT deliveries/delivery_items; calculate next batch_no
DB --> Repo: prior state and issued quantities
Issue -> Stock: getStockSummary(variantId)
Stock -> DB: Read WH_MAIN inventory
DB --> Stock: inventoryId
Issue -> Catalog: getSkuSummary(variantId)
Catalog -> DB: Read serial tracking flag
DB --> Catalog: not serial-tracked
Issue -> Repo: save Delivery(DRAFT) + DeliveryItem rows
Repo -> DB: INSERT deliveries; INSERT delivery_items\n(transaction; draft does not consume stock)
DB --> Repo: generated/accepted rows
Issue --> Ctrl: Result(deliveryId, batchNo, DRAFT)
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<Result>
UI --> User: Show saved draft

== UC-39: confirm issue atomically ==
User -> UI: Confirm issue
UI -> Sec: POST /deliveries/{id}/confirm-issue
Sec -> Ctrl: Authorized request
Ctrl -> Issue: confirm(deliveryId)
Issue -> IAM: getCurrentUser()
Issue -> Repo: Read delivery scalar orderId; lock order then delivery
Repo -> DB: SELECT orderId; lock Sales order; SELECT delivery FOR UPDATE
DB --> Repo: Locked order + delivery
Issue -> Sales: lockInvoice(invoiceId); revalidate PROCESSING order and issued totals
Sales -> DB: Read/lock invoice and order lines
DB --> Sales: current invoice/order quantities
Issue -> Finance: available(orderId, existing COD commitments)
Finance -> DB: Read verified receipts, pending COD and commitments\nunder Finance consistency rules
DB --> Finance: available COD amount
Issue -> Stock: Validate own held + free stock; issue(command per DeliveryItemId)
Stock -> DB: Lock inventory/reservations; consume only this order's hold/free units;\nwrite stock movement idempotently by deliveryItemId
DB --> Stock: inventory movement results
Issue -> Repo: Set confirmedBy/confirmedAt/dispatchDate; status DISPATCHED
Repo -> DB: UPDATE deliveries; commit transaction
DB --> Repo: Commit
Issue --> Ctrl: confirmed Result
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<Result>
UI --> User: Show DISPATCHED / issue note available
note over Issue,DB
Any line, quantity, reservation, COD, or stock error rolls back the transaction.
No invoice issuance, order/payment completion, or automatic restock occurs here.
end note

== UC-40: list and assign/reassign one delivery per order batch ==
User -> UI: Filter deliveries / assign selected delivery IDs to active shipper
UI -> Sec: GET /deliveries or PUT /delivery-assignments
Sec -> Ctrl: ACCOUNTANT / SHOP_OWNER authorized
Ctrl -> DeliverySvc: search(...) or assign(request)
DeliverySvc -> IAM: getCurrentUser(); getUserById(shipperId)
IAM --> DeliverySvc: role/actor and active SHIPPER summary
DeliverySvc -> Repo: Lock selected Delivery rows in sorted ID order
Repo -> DB: SELECT deliveries FOR UPDATE
DB --> Repo: DISPATCHED / ASSIGNED / eligible RESCHEDULED rows
DeliverySvc -> Repo: Update shipperId, assignedBy, assignedAt, status
Repo -> DB: UPDATE deliveries; flush; commit assignment transaction
DB --> Repo: Updated rows
DeliverySvc --> Ctrl: Summary list
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<List<Summary>>
UI --> User: Show assignments
note over DeliverySvc,DB
Assignment acts on individual delivery records. No trip, vehicle, route, or stop table is created.
end note

== UC-41: shipper starts, reschedules, fails, or completes delivery ==
User -> UI: Open assigned-delivery action
UI -> Sec: POST /deliveries/{id}/start | reschedule | fail | complete
Sec -> Ctrl: SHIPPER role authorized; JWT user bound to request
Ctrl -> DeliverySvc: start/reschedule/fail/complete(id, payload)
DeliverySvc -> IAM: getCurrentUser()
IAM --> DeliverySvc: authenticated shipper UUID
DeliverySvc -> Repo: lockById(deliveryId); verify delivery.shipperId == actor
Repo -> DB: SELECT delivery FOR UPDATE
DB --> Repo: current state and assignment
alt Start or resume
  DeliverySvc -> Repo: ASSIGNED/RESCHEDULED -> IN_TRANSIT; preserve first startedAt
  Repo -> DB: UPDATE deliveries; commit
else Temporary obstacle
  DeliverySvc -> Repo: append reason/date; status RESCHEDULED
  Repo -> DB: UPDATE deliveries; commit
else Confirmed cancellation/refusal
  DeliverySvc -> Repo: require explicit confirmation + reason; status FAILED
  Repo -> DB: UPDATE deliveries; commit (no inventory restock)
else Successful handover with photos
  DeliverySvc -> DeliverySvc: Validate 1..5 image files (type, bytes, decoder)
  DeliverySvc -> Photos: store image bytes
  Photos --> DeliverySvc: private storage keys
  DeliverySvc -> Repo: lockById + recheck ownership/state
  Repo -> DB: SELECT delivery FOR UPDATE
  DB --> Repo: IN_TRANSIT delivery
  DeliverySvc -> Repo: store photo metadata JSONB; set deliveredAt; status DELIVERED
  Repo -> DB: UPDATE deliveries; commit
  alt Database update fails or race lost
    DeliverySvc -> Photos: delete staged files (compensating cleanup)
  end
end
DeliverySvc --> Ctrl: Delivery Summary
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<Summary>
UI --> User: Show updated status
note over DeliverySvc,DB
Delivery outcome does not complete/pay the sales order, settle COD, or alter inventory.
COD settlement belongs to UC-30; returned-goods receipt/restock belongs to UC-37.
end note

== UC-42: authorized detail, status, timestamps, items and photo ==
User -> UI: Open delivery or order delivery history
UI -> Sec: GET /deliveries/{id} or GET /orders/{orderId}/deliveries
Sec -> Ctrl: JWT role authorized
Ctrl -> DeliverySvc: detail(id) or byOrder(orderId)
DeliverySvc -> Repo: Read delivery + DeliveryItem rows
Repo -> DB: SELECT deliveries; SELECT delivery_items\n(paginated for byOrder)
DB --> Repo: delivery records and item IDs
DeliverySvc -> IAM: getCurrentUser(); assigned shipper lookup when needed
IAM --> DeliverySvc: role/ownership and shipper summary
DeliverySvc -> Catalog: getSkuSummaries(variantIds)
Catalog -> DB: Read SKU display fields
DB --> Catalog: SKU summaries
DeliverySvc -> DeliverySvc: Authorize ACCOUNTANT/SHOP_OWNER\nor only the currently assigned SHIPPER
DeliverySvc --> Ctrl: Detail/Summary projection
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<Detail/Page<Summary>>
UI --> User: Render state, timestamps, items, photos
opt Read photo content URL
  User -> UI: Open photo
  UI -> Sec: GET /deliveries/{id}/photos/{photoId}
  Sec -> Ctrl: JWT role authorized
  Ctrl -> DeliverySvc: readPhoto(id, photoId)
  DeliverySvc -> Repo: Read delivery JSONB photo metadata; check object ownership
  Repo -> DB: SELECT deliveries.proof_photos
  DB --> Repo: photoId + private storage key
  DeliverySvc -> Photos: read(private storage key)
  Photos --> DeliverySvc: image bytes + MIME
  DeliverySvc --> Ctrl: bytes (no-store, nosniff)
  Ctrl --> UI: Image response
end

== UC-43: shipper reads only own assigned deliveries ==
User -> UI: Open My Deliveries; optionally filter status/date/page
UI -> Sec: GET /me/deliveries
Sec -> Ctrl: SHIPPER role authorized
Ctrl -> DeliverySvc: mine(status, scheduledFrom, scheduledTo, pageable)
DeliverySvc -> IAM: getCurrentUser()
IAM --> DeliverySvc: authenticated shipper UUID
DeliverySvc -> Repo: Query by shipperId = current actor (never client-supplied)
Repo -> DB: SELECT deliveries WHERE shipper_id = actor\n+filters + pagination
DB --> Repo: Assigned Delivery summaries
DeliverySvc --> Ctrl: Page<Summary>
Ctrl --> UI: ApiResponse<Page<Summary>>
UI --> User: Show assigned deliveries

@enduml
